{"game_id":2026020357,"away":"VAN","home":"SEA","split":{"name":"Gallagher","side":0,"sec":1890},"lede":"Seattle had last change, so Lane Lambert picked most of these matchups. Seattle played without Jani Nyman and Ville Ottavainen. Vancouver lost Brendan Gallagher after 11:30 of the second.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Stephenson’s line drew E. Pettersson’s line","text":"Lane Lambert sent Stephenson, Gaudreau and Winterton out for 9:59 of their 15:07 at 5-on-5 against DeBrusk, E. Pettersson and Lekkerimäki (66%, about 28% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.26 to 0.20 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"Beniers’s line drew Boeser’s line","text":"Kakko, Beniers and Samoskevich spent 9:32 of their 13:53 at 5-on-5 against Cotter, Chytil and Boeser (69%, about 33% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 1.20 to 0.36 expected goals. Seattle scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Karlsson’s line","text":"McMann, Catton and Eberle spent 5:19 of their 9:55 at 5-on-5 against Öhgren, Rossi and Karlsson (54%, about 28% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.32 to 0.02 expected goals. Seattle scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Gallagher left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"Boeser dropped from 29% to 21% of Vancouver’s 5-on-5 time. The matchups stayed: Beniers’s line against Vancouver’s second line (68% before, 69% after) and Stephenson’s line against Vancouver’s first line (63% before, 69% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Vancouver had 0.70 to 2.70 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Gallagher left and 0.62 to 0.74 after. Vancouver trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Lane Lambert matched harder than in his other home games: each line spent 60% of its time against one opposing line, against 3